OL,3,GNEWSACaptain in UK's worst helicopter
OL,4,Acrash recalls 1986 tragedy
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man who captained a helicopter which
OL,7,Fcrashed with the loss of dozens of
OL,8,Flives 40 years ago has told how he
OL,9,Fcould not comprehend he was one of only
OL,10,Ftwo survivors.
OL,12,FThe Chinook carrying offshore workers
OL,13,Fcrashed into the North Sea after a
OL,14,Fcatastrophic gear box failure off the
OL,15,Fcoast of Shetland on 6 November 1986.
OL,17,FForty-three passengers and two crew
OL,18,Fmembers died, while one passenger
OL,19,Fsurvived alongside Captain Pushp Vaid.
OL,20,FIt remains the UK's worst helicopter
OL,21,Faccident.
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
